{
    "background_story": "Wayne was a seasoned coal miner who spent most of his life underground. He took great pride in his work, ensuring the safety of his crew and the efficiency of their operations. One of his most important tasks was maintaining the brattice, a critical ventilation system that kept the air clean and breathable in the mine. Wayne's attention to detail and expertise in repairing the brattice earned him the respect of his peers. During a particularly hazardous gas leak, Wayne's quick thinking and knowledge of the brattice system allowed him to redirect airflow and prevent a disaster. His bravery and expertise saved countless lives, and he became a hero in the mining community. Wayne's dedication to his craft and his crew was unwavering, a testament to the importance of skilled miners like him.",
